# GitHub Release Workflow

Use when the user asks to create a release, tag, or publish. Changelog writing stays in `changelog.mdc`; commit/PR conventions in `contributing.mdc`. This rule covers tagging and `gh release` only.

## Prerequisites

Before tagging:

1. Changelog exists at `docs/community/changelog/<MAJOR>/<version>.md` with indexes updated per `changelog.mdc`
2. Feature work and `docs(changelog): update changelog for version <version>` are committed
3. User has **accepted** the changelog draft

Do not create a tag or GitHub release until the user accepts the changelog.

## Push Then Release

```bash
git push -u origin HEAD
# Retry SSH if the remote drops the connection
```

Tag format: `X.Y.Z` — **no** `v` prefix. Matches `.github/workflows/publish.yml` (`on.push.tags: '[0-9]+.[0-9]+.[0-9]+'`).

## Create Release

Strip YAML frontmatter, H1 (`# X.Y.Z — date`), and nav links. Body must start at the first `##` section (usually `## Added`), matching prior releases (e.g. 4.17.1).

```bash
# ✅ GOOD — title is version only; notes start at ## Added
tmp=$(mktemp)
sed -n '/^## /,$p' docs/community/changelog/<MAJOR>/<version>.md > "$tmp"
gh release create <version> --title "<version>" --notes-file "$tmp" --latest
rm "$tmp"
```

```text
# ❌ BAD — do not paste the changelog file as-is
---
title: "Changelog 4.18.0"
description: "Release notes for ArchiPy 4.18.0"
---
# 4.18.0 — 2026-08-02
[4.17.1 →](4.17.1.md) | [↑ 4.x series](index.md)
```

## Verify

```bash
gh release view <version>
gh run list --workflow=publish.yml --limit 1
```

Confirm the release URL and that the publish workflow started.

## Fix Wrong Notes

```bash
tmp=$(mktemp)
sed -n '/^## /,$p' docs/community/changelog/<MAJOR>/<version>.md > "$tmp"
gh release edit <version> --notes-file "$tmp"
rm "$tmp"
```
